From: computerguy526 <355510486+computerguy526@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 21:19:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 22/22] kosmickrisp: MetalFX bridge: depth-from-colour.w prep
 kernel (motion RG16F + R32F depth), output-usage fallback, idle
 scaler/texture release

Temporal with no depth image: a prep compute pass writes the motion vectors as
RG16F and depth_near / colour.w as reversed device depth. Output images whose
usage MetalFX refuses go through a bridge texture and a copy. Scalers and bridge
textures unused for FX_IDLE (600) calls are released after being made
non-resident (the resident callback gets an unresident pair), so the loading
screen's dynamic-resolution sizes do not pile up.
